PART 2: STATE MANAGEMENT COMPLETE WORKFLOW
================================================================================

COMPLETE STATE MANAGEMENT WORKFLOW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 1: DEFINE STATE

• Identify information that must change over time

• Determine the initial value

• Decide the appropriate state shape

        ↓

STEP 2: CREATE STATE

import { useState } from 'react'

const [state, setState] =
  useState(initialValue)

        ↓

STEP 3: RENDER USING STATE

• Read state during rendering

• Use state in JSX

• Display the current application state

        ↓

STEP 4: HANDLE USER INTERACTION

• Attach event handlers

• Capture user interaction/input

• Determine the next state

        ↓

STEP 5: UPDATE STATE

• Do not mutate existing state

• Create the next value/object/array

• Call the state setter

        ↓

STEP 6: REACT PROCESSES THE UPDATE

• React receives/queues the update

• Determines the next state

• May skip unnecessary work when state is effectively unchanged

        ↓

STEP 7: COMPONENT RE-RENDERS

• Component function executes again when needed

• Updated state is available

• JSX is reevaluated

        ↓

STEP 8: RECONCILIATION

• React compares the previous and new rendered output

• Determines which UI changes are required

        ↓

STEP 9: COMMIT

• Required DOM changes are applied

        ↓

STEP 10: DISPLAY UPDATED

• User sees the resulting UI

• Application is ready for the next interaction


WORKFLOW TABLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+------+--------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+
| STEP | ACTION             | INPUT                | RESULT                     |
+------+--------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+
| 1    | Define State       | Requirements         | State plan                 |
| 2    | Create State       | Initial value        | [state, setter]            |
| 3    | Render             | Current state        | JSX                        |
| 4    | Handle Interaction | User action          | Event handler              |
| 5    | Update State       | Next value           | Setter called              |
| 6    | Process Update     | State update         | Next state determined      |
| 7    | Re-render          | Current state        | New rendered output        |
| 8    | Reconcile          | Previous/new output  | Required differences       |
| 9    | Commit             | Required changes     | DOM updated as necessary   |
| 10   | Display            | Updated DOM          | User sees current UI       |
+------+--------------------+----------------------+----------------------------+


ONE-LINE FLOW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

User Action
    ↓
Event Handler
    ↓
State Setter
    ↓
React Processes State
    ↓
Render
    ↓
Reconciliation
    ↓
DOM Commit
    ↓
Updated UI


