================================================================================
CRITICAL STATE MANAGEMENT POINTS
================================================================================

• useState manages local component state

• State should be treated as read-only

• Use setters to request state updates

• Create new objects/arrays instead of mutating existing ones

• Use functional updates when next state depends on previous state

• Keep state minimal

• Avoid duplicating derived information

• Keep state close to the component that owns it

• Group or split state based on relationships and update behavior

• Handle loading, success, empty, and error states

• Test application behavior from the user's perspective

• Profile before adding performance optimizations

• Use Context when appropriate, not automatically

• Move to useReducer when transitions become complex


