+------------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| CONCEPT                | REMEMBER                                      |
+------------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| State                  | Data React remembers for component            |
| useState               | Local state Hook                              |
| Setter                 | Requests next state                           |
| State Snapshot         | Each render sees its own current values       |
| Immutability           | Don't modify existing state                   |
| Object Reference       | Identity matters for objects/arrays           |
| Functional Update      | setter(previous => next)                      |
| Derived State          | Calculate when possible                       |
| Re-render              | Component executes again                      |
| Reconciliation         | React determines UI differences               |
| Commit                 | Necessary DOM changes                         |
| Batching               | React can process updates together            |
| State Ownership        | Keep state near its owner                     |
| State Isolation        | Component instances have independent state    |
| Props                  | Parent-provided component inputs              |
| Context                | Share appropriate data deeper in tree         |
| useReducer             | Useful for complex transitions                |
